---
title: "Tax filing deadline extension: Biztax by 15 October, personal income tax returns with specific income by 31 October"
date: 2026-10-06
lang: en
category: Tax
excerpt: "In response to technical difficulties with tax platforms, new deadlines give directors additional time: 15 October for Biztax, 31 October for Tax-on-web with specific income."
published: true
author: AgiFid
---

Following consultations between the ITAA, the cabinet of Finance Minister Jan Jambon and the FPS Finance, two deadlines have been set for the end of the 2026 tax season.

Biztax returns may be filed until 15 October 2026, whilst personal income tax returns including specific income may be filed until 31 October 2026.

This extension responds directly to the difficulties encountered on tax platforms, which have marked the entire 2026 season.

## Two separate dates to limit saturation

The initial deadline for Biztax returns was set at 30 September 2026, whilst that for personal income tax returns with specific income was 16 October 2026.

The decision to retain two dates follows operational logic: concentrating several deadlines on the same day increases the pressure exerted on platforms at the most critical moment. The staggered approach aims to avoid further overload in the final days, a scenario which had already occurred last July.

As a reminder, specific income includes: profits from self-employed individuals operating as sole traders, remuneration of company directors, remuneration of assisting spouses and foreign professional income.

## A tax season under pressure

By 16 September, 316,646 returns had already been filed via Biztax, more than 10% higher than the previous year according to FPS Finance figures. Yet despite this progress, the persistent technical difficulties encountered within various tax platforms have justified the extension of deadlines.

On 14 September, Minister Jan Jambon and the ITAA presidency agreed to work together on the difficulties encountered with tax platforms, via a tripartite working group bringing together the ITAA, the FPS Finance and the minister's cabinet.

## A further extension remains possible

If these new deadlines are not sufficient, you may request a further extension from the FPS Finance in cases of force majeure or serious grounds, and if several clients are affected for the same reason, a single grouped request is sufficient.

## What this changes for your practice

For AgiFid, this extension directly modifies October's schedule. Files in progress benefit from a 15-day margin for Biztax. However, be aware: these deadlines are a safety net, not a target. The earlier returns arrive, the lower the risk of Biztax and Tax-on-web Mandataire becoming saturated as the deadlines approach.

Another important point: a return filed earlier will not advance any potential audit, as confirmed by Minister Jan Jambon.

The message therefore remains clear: file as soon as the case is ready, without waiting until the final days. The remainder of the tax season depends largely on the collective capacity to spread filings over time.
